WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.288
Let’s walk through Read queue state.

00:00:02.288 --> 00:00:05.075
Start with the badge, pending count, reviewed-history state

00:00:05.075 --> 00:00:06.537
, and refresh result.

00:00:06.537 --> 00:00:09.650
Determine whether work is pending, dependency-locked, empty,

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.250
or already reviewed before opening a card or choosing a

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.250
decision.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.675
On this slide, the queue badge, pending count

00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:18.525
, reviewed-history controls, and Refresh action show what is

00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:20.488
ready for this specialist seat.

00:00:20.488 --> 00:00:24.262
In practice, refresh deliberately when coordinating a handoff;

00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:27.438
background refresh does not decide an outcome or clear an

00:00:27.438 --> 00:00:28.663
unread item.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.922
Before you continue, verify these points:

00:00:31.922 --> 00:00:35.010
Pending means the seat still requires action.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.197
Locked or empty rows are not approval failures.

00:00:38.197 --> 00:00:40.460
Reviewed history remains read-only.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.435
When you are ready, use Open SME queue to

00:00:43.435 --> 00:00:45.210
move to the live surface.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.985
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:47.985 --> 00:00:48.135
.
